    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "The frai-core test suite is now fully passing with all 28 tests working correctly. I've fixed the two failing tests:\n\n**Issue 1: governance.test.js** \u2013 The test imports `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export. I added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` in the governance module.\n\n**Issue 2: eval/index.test.js** \u2013 The `toxicityMetric` function signature only accepted `(outputs, bannedTerms)`, but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`. This caused the references array to be misinterpreted as banned terms, flagging all samples. I fixed the signature to accept `(outputs, references, bannedTerms)` to match the pattern of other metrics.",
